      "message": "hi @Emily Wachowiak @Eric Pang ! I've reviewed the theme names and my notes can be found below:\n\n* the following theme names scored 'low', meaning they're considered college level for readability: Nova, Ember, Smolder, Moonrise / I'd consider changing these if possible\n* I understand the use in Nova but I'm concerned users who have low vision or are colorblind may not know what color to associate with this\n* Flare scores well for readability, but I have a slight concern that it could be associated with red or orange too instead of pink\n\nHere are words I've found and checked for Ember, Smolder, and Moonrise:\n* Ember- gold, straw\n* Smolder- violet, plum, jam, jelly\n* Moonrise- sky, ocean\n(note: the words above are not required to use, just suggestions. if there are different theme names you'd like to use and have checked, just let me know!)\n\nif you have any questions, please reach out! thank you!",
